  "worked_solution": "We want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{31}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $1$st row of $A$ multiplied by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{31}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{1},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{31}=-(-1)=1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
